  "premise": "Twenty-four hours after Narrow Furnace, the intact convoy completes its westward passage while BLUE launches a coordinated carrier and land-based attack on the remaining coastal kill chain. RED commits both rested Shahin F-14As and every surviving surface raider in a simultaneous counterstroke. The result is a compressed three-axis fight: counter-air over the Strait, surface action around the convoy lanes, and suppression of the Bastion and S-300 belt.",
  "blue_intent": "Use Tiger as the flexible carrier element, Viper for precision suppression, and both P-8s for maritime targeting. Protect the carrier and at least four auxiliaries while striking the coastal-missile, air-defense, and surface-raider groups in parallel.",
  "red_intent": "Launch Shahin immediately to contest the air picture, drive the six surviving raiders into converging attack lanes, and coordinate their pressure with the Bastion and S-300 batteries against BLUE high-value units.",
  "escalation_constraints": [
    "BLUE attacks remain limited to forces actively controlling or attacking the Hormuz corridor.",
    "Bandar Abbas Strip itself is not a preplanned target, although launched Shahin aircraft may be engaged.",
    "Civilian and neutral traffic remains outside the engagement authorization.",
    "Neither side is authorized to employ nuclear weapons."
  ],
